course: dictionary
lesson: 8795
title: Who owns a company?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A company is a business, and it can be split into small parts called shares. A person who owns shares is a shareholder. A shareholder is a part-owner: they own a piece of the business, not the whole of it.
explain: «A share is a small piece of a company; owning 1 share out of 100 means owning 1 hundredth of it, and a shareholder gets a part of the profits.» So if you own 1 share out of 100, you own one hundredth of the company, and you get one hundredth of its profits.
explain: Shareholders often hope the company does well, because then their shares can grow in value. A shareholder who receives part of the profits gets dividends. Shareholders can also vote at meetings about the company.
fact: A shareholder is a person or organisation that owns shares in a company.
fact: A share is a small piece of a company, so each share is a tiny part of its ownership.
fact: A shareholder may get dividends, which are their part of the company's profits.
fact: If a profit of £1,000 is shared equally among 4 shareholders, each one gets £250.
fact: A major shareholder is someone who owns a large number of shares.
exercise: «A share is a small piece of a company.» What is a shareholder? | *A person or organisation that owns shares in a company | A company that sells its shares to nobody | A profit that a company keeps in a box | A person who works in a shop
exercise: «Owning 1 share out of 100 means owning 1 hundredth of it.» If you own 1 share out of 100, what part of the company do you own? | *One hundredth | Half of the company | One tenth | All of the company
exercise: A profit of £1,000 is shared equally among 4 shareholders. How much does each shareholder get? | £1,004 | *£250 | £400 | £25
test: What are dividends? | The price of one share on its first day | Words for the company's buildings | *A shareholder's part of the company's profits | A vote at a shareholders' meeting
test: At a shareholders' meeting, what do shareholders do? | They close the company for ever | *They vote on things that affect the company | They sing songs about the company | They bake cakes for the staff
exam: Which phrase means a shareholder who owns a large number of shares? | *Major shareholder | Share price | Shareholders' meeting | Shareholder vote
